    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nsurround\n\n### Description\n\nThe docs online say:\r\n```\r\n- `saiwi[[<CR>]]<CR>` - add (`sa`) for inner word (`iw`) interactive\r\n  surrounding (`i`): `[[` for left and `]]` for right.\r\n```\r\nand indeed, it worked this way in the past. However, it appear that the default is now:\r\n```\r\n- `saiw?[[<CR>]]<CR>` - add (`sa`) for inner word (`iw`) interactive\r\n  surrounding (`?`): `[[` for left and `]]` for right.\r\n```\r\nWhich of these are intended?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. enter `saiwi` and see it surround the word with `i` and not go into interactive mode\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. enter `saiwi` and see it go into interactive mode\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. enter `saiwi` and see it surround the word with `i` and not go into interactive mode",
